# The vendored terminal engine's bundle IS committed, despite being a `dist/` (#6).
#
# It is a build output that is also a dependency: `vendor/ghostty-web-patched/package.json` points
# `main`/`module`/`types`/`exports` into `dist/`, the root override installs that directory as
# `ghostty-web`, and pnpm COPIES a `file:` dependency into its store at install time. While the
# bundle was ignored, a fresh clone installed an empty package, `pnpm typecheck` failed with
# TS2307 ("Cannot find module 'ghostty-web'"), every `App.*` suite failed to load, and the only
# repair was a hand-run rebuild plus a second install, a build that a clone cannot perform from
# what the clone contains, since the bundle's own toolchain is not in this workspace's lockfile.
# Tracking it makes `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` sufficient. It is regenerated, not edited:
# `pnpm vendor:build` rebuilds it from the tracked `source/` snapshot and the tracked
# `ghostty-vt.wasm`, and `packages/client/src/terminal/vendor-engine.test.ts` guards what lands.
!vendor/ghostty-web-patched/dist/
# vendor:build stages the rebuilt bundle here before renaming it over dist/; never tracked.
vendor/ghostty-web-patched/dist.new/

# The living specs in docs/ ARE committed: 106 comments across 81 source files cite them by
# section as the normative behaviour, and `pnpm test` checks the wire protocol against
# docs/wire-protocol.md. A spec the repo does not carry cannot be reviewed beside the change
# that alters it, and a fresh clone could not run the suite at all.
#
# What stays out is the parity campaign's records and the audit artifacts. The campaign docs
# (PARITY, UI-FIDELITY, SPACING-REVIEW, MOBILE-*, PLAN-retired, compat-status, capabilities/,
# research/) now live OUTSIDE the repo, at ../kelpi-docs, and are referenced by hand. Only the
# generated audit output still lands under docs/, so only it is ignored here.
docs/audit/
